# Byte-exact checkouts.
#
# This repository carries a content manifest (manifest.sha256 / INTEGRITY.md) whose
# values are SHA-256 over the *bytes on disk*. Git's default end-of-line translation
# rewrites files on checkout: a file committed with LF on Windows is checked out as
# CRLF, the bytes differ, and every digest in the manifest becomes wrong — on one
# platform only, which is the worst kind of wrong.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL translation, so the bytes in a checkout are the bytes that
# were committed, on every platform. Git is then a byte transport, which is what a
# manifest requires.
#
# If you add a genuine binary file, it is already covered: `-text` is the correct
# setting for it too.
* -text
